+//! Locking the session.
+//!
+//! A window of this kind is one of the surfaces a compositor shows while the
+//! session is locked, in place of everything else. The protocol
+//! (`ext-session-lock-v1`) is the only way to lock a Wayland session
+//! honestly: the compositor stops showing anything else the moment the lock
+//! is taken, and goes on hiding it even if the locker dies, so a crash
+//! cannot leave the desktop open.
+//!
+//! One window per screen. The compositor decides their size, and a locker is
+//! expected to fill every screen there is: a screen with no lock surface on
+//! it is shown as a blank.
+
+use thiserror::Error;
+
+/// Options for a window that is part of a session lock. There is nothing to
+/// choose: the size is the screen's, and which screen it is comes from
+/// [`crate::WindowOptions::display_id`].
+#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]
+pub struct SessionLockOptions {}
+
+/// An error indicating that an action failed because the compositor doesn't support the required
+/// session lock protocol.
+#[derive(Debug, Error)]
+#[error("Compositor doesn't support ext_session_lock_v1")]
+pub struct SessionLockNotSupportedError;
